@startuml UploadCVAndAutoParsing
title 3.2.2.1 Upload CV & Auto Parsing via Python AI Service
skinparam monochrome true
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam maxMessageSize 260
hide footbox

<style>
sequenceDiagram {
  groupHeader {
    FontStyle plain
  }
}
</style>
autonumber

' Sources: supplied report, section IV.3.2.2.1 and Workflow 2: Manage Profile and CV.
' Implementation: UserController.uploadCv, UserServiceImpl.upCv,
' ApiClientImpl.sendChatToAnythingLlm, CandidateProfileImpl, EventListenerHandle.handleCv.
' Reviewed local Inblue-BE master and EXE_FE on 2026-09-18.
' Diagram shows the current implementation, not the legacy TestController Python endpoint.

actor Candidate
participant "Web UI\nCVUploadModal / AccountPage" as UI
participant ":UserController" as Controller
participant ":UserServiceImpl" as Service
participant ":UserRepository" as Users
participant ":CandidateProfileImpl" as Profiles
participant ":CandidateProfileRepository" as ProfileRepo
participant ":ApiClientImpl" as API
participant "AnythingLLM\nCV_PARSE workspace" as AI
participant ":EventListenerHandle" as Listener
participant "Cloudinary\nvia CloudinaryService" as Storage

note over API, AI
  Report heading retained as requested.
  Current upload flow calls AnythingLLM directly.
  Python /api/v1/parse-cv is called only by a test endpoint;
  it is not invoked by UserServiceImpl.upCv().
end note

Candidate -> UI : Select CV file
UI -> UI : Validate PDF type/extension and size <= 10 MB
break [File type is invalid or file size exceeds the limit]
  UI --> Candidate : Show validation error
end
UI --> Candidate : Preview selected PDF
Candidate -> UI : Confirm upload
UI -> Controller : POST /api/users/upload-cv\n multipart: userId, cvFile, [applicationId]
activate Controller
note over UI, Controller
  Account UI sends userId and cvFile only.
  applicationId is an optional backend parameter.
  Precondition: authenticated request accepted by security filters.
end note
Controller -> Service : upCv(userId, applicationId, cvFile)
activate Service

break [CV file is empty (direct API request)]
  Service --> Controller : null
  Controller --> UI : HTTP 200, empty body
end

group Transactional upCv attempt
  Service -> Users : findById(userId)
  activate Users
  Users --> Service : User (or absent)
  deactivate Users
  note right of Service
    Missing user throws RuntimeException.
    Synchronous exceptions trigger retry of the entire
    upCv call: max 3 attempts, 2-second backoff.
    Empty/invalid AI output also leads to failure.
    After exhaustion, recover() throws;
    GlobalExceptionHandler returns HTTP 500.
    The UI shows an upload error.
    Cloudinary side effects are not rolled back.
  end note

  opt [User has an existing CV public ID]
    Service -> Storage : deletePdf(user.cv_public_id)
    Storage --> Service : Deletion result
  end

  alt [Application ID is provided]
    Service -> Profiles : getProfileByApplicationId(applicationId)
    Profiles -> ProfileRepo : findByApplicationId(applicationId)
    ProfileRepo --> Profiles : Existing profile or null
    Profiles --> Service : Existing profile or null
  else [Application ID is not provided]
    Service -> Profiles : getProfileByUserIdAndApplicationIdIsNull(userId)
    Profiles -> ProfileRepo : findByUser_IdAndApplicationIdIsNull(userId)
    ProfileRepo --> Profiles : Existing profile or null
    Profiles --> Service : Existing profile or null
  end
  Service -> Service : Reuse existing profile ID, otherwise null

  Service -> API : sendChatToAnythingLlm(CV_PARSE, null,\n"parse-cv", true, [cvFile], CVParserResponse.class)
  activate API
  API -> API : Encode CV as Base64 attachment\nBuild JSON body and bearer-auth header
  API -> AI : POST {ANYTHING_LLM_URL}/workspace/parse-cv/chat\nmode=chat, sessionId=parse-cv, reset=true, attachments
  activate AI
  AI --> API : textResponse (structured profile JSON), metrics
  deactivate AI
  API -> API : Remove Markdown fences; save chat log via\nLlmChatLogService; deserialize CVParserResponse
  API --> Service : CVParserResponse
  deactivate API

  Service -> Service : Build CandidateProfile with user/application\nMap skills, projects, experience, education,\ncertifications, achievements and target role/level
  note right of Service
    GPA normalization: 10-point score x 0.4;
    4-point score unchanged; invalid value -> 0.0.
  end note
  Service -> Service : Prepare detached MultipartFile via FileUtil\nDelete temporary file
  Service -> Profiles : createProfile(candidateProfile)
  activate Profiles
  Profiles -> ProfileRepo : save(candidateProfile)
  activate ProfileRepo
  ProfileRepo --> Profiles : Saved profile (insert or update)
  deactivate ProfileRepo
  Profiles --> Service : Saved profile
  deactivate Profiles
  Service ->> Listener : publishEvent(UserEventDto(user, file, "cv"))\nvia ApplicationEventPublisher / @Async
end

par Return parsed profile (does not wait for Cloudinary)
  Service --> Controller : CandidateProfile (transaction completes)
  deactivate Service
  Controller --> UI : HTTP 200 + CandidateProfile
  deactivate Controller
  UI -> UI : Refresh account data
  UI --> Candidate : Show upload success and close modal
else [CV is being stored in background]
  activate Listener
  Listener -> Users : findById(user.id)
  Users --> Listener : User or null
  opt [User still exists]
    opt [Existing CV public ID is present]
      Listener -> Storage : deletePdf(user.cv_public_id)
      Storage --> Listener : Deletion result
    end
    Listener -> Storage : uploadDocument(file)
    Storage --> Listener : secure_url, public_id
    Listener -> Listener : Set user.cvUrl and user.cv_public_id
    Listener -> Users : save(user)
    Users --> Listener : Updated user
  end
  deactivate Listener
end

note over UI, Storage
  Background storage may finish before or after the HTTP response.
  Its failure does not change an already returned HTTP 200;
  an immediate account refresh may still show the previous CV URL.
end note
@enduml
